# Main Branch Rule

All project work is committed and pushed directly to the `main` branch.

## Rules

- Commit changes on `main` and push with `git push origin main`.
- Do not create feature, topic, or temporary branches.
- If a branch other than `main` was created by mistake, merge its work into `main`, push, then delete the extra branch locally and on the remote.
- Pull the latest `main` (`git pull origin main`) before committing to avoid conflicts.
